(# Strong induction restated) Tj T*
(Strong induction proves a property for every natural number at or above the) Tj T*
(base case by assuming the property holds for every value strictly below n,) Tj T*
(rather than only for n minus one. It is a convenience and not a stronger axiom:) Tj T*
(any proof written with strong induction can be rewritten as ordinary induction) Tj T*
(over a modified predicate. The base case is not a formality. A proof with a false) Tj T*
(base case establishes nothing at all, however clean the inductive step looks on) Tj T*
(the page. Use the strong form when the recursion in the problem reaches back more) Tj T*
(than a single step, which is the usual situation for divide and conquer) Tj T*
(recurrences. Ordinary induction hands you one previous case; strong induction) Tj T*
(hands you all of them.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
