(# The well-ordering principle) Tj T*
(Every non-empty set of natural numbers has a least element. This principle is) Tj T*
(logically equivalent to induction and is often taken as the primitive instead,) Tj T*
(with induction derived from it as a theorem about minimal counterexamples.) Tj T*
ET
