(# A long historical digression) Tj T*
(The modern statement of induction is usually credited to Pascal and Fermat, though) Tj T*
(arguments of the same shape appear far earlier in Euclid and in the work of the) Tj T*
(Indian mathematician Bhaskara. Formal treatment waited for Dedekind and Peano, who) Tj T*
(made induction an axiom of arithmetic rather than a technique of proof. The history) Tj T*
(matters less than the practice, but the vocabulary of the field still carries traces) Tj T*
(of the older debate about whether induction is discovered or stipulated. Students) Tj T*
(encountering the axiom for the first time often ask which it is, and the honest) Tj T*
(answer is that for arithmetic as we use it the question has no operational content.) Tj T*
ET
